   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Introducing yourself",
     "texto": [
      "**Nazywam się Anna** and **Mam na imię Tom** are used to say your name. In **mam na imię**, the natural translation is «my name is»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Origin and where you live",
     "texto": [
      "To say where you are from: **Jestem z Polski** or **Jestem z Hiszpanii**. After **z**, the country name changes form.",
      "To say where you live, we use **w**: **Mieszkam w Warszawie**. To name a language, you say **po polsku** or **po hiszpańsku**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "People and verbs",
     "texto": [
      "In Polish, the pronoun «I» is usually left out, because the verb ending gives that information: **mówię** = «I speak», **mówisz** = «you speak».",
      "**Uczę się polskiego** means «I study/learn Polish»; in this expression, **polskiego** changes form."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
